  "summary": "Consume native device ContactPlan bounds in contact persistence and preparation dispatches.",
  "regressions": [
    "The existing native cases now launch through padded storage while consuming the actual device bound, including empty contacts and 31/32/33/63/64/65/129 tails.",
    "Plan uniforms and guard records remain bitwise unchanged, and invalid counts or launch capacities fail validation.",
    "The supplied-manifold TGS program supplies the same native plan buffer without changing its physics or color schedule."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "A Plan buffer is added to the TileLang contact and link launch ABI to match the native Rust shader uniform; the prior adapters specialized its bound from host fixture metadata.",
    "No CPU readback or host contact-count substitution is required between collision generation and these stages.",
    "This prepares scene composition; production simulation integration and hardware qualification remain unfinished."
  ],
